2. SUBMISSIONS:
A. The Insurer repudiated ₹60,000 alleging non-disclosure of hypertension under Clause 4.2.
B. However, at the time of admission, the policy was in its 6th continuous year (64 months active cover).
C. Policy Clause 5.4 unambiguously mandates:
"After 60 continuous months of coverage have been completed, no claim shall be contestable by the Insurer on grounds of non-disclosure or misrepresentation, except for proven fraud."
D. The Insurer failed to honour this clause before their GRO and failed to resolve the matter within statutory timelines.

3. RELIEF SOUGHT:
The Complainant prays for an Award directing the Insurer to:
1. Pay the withheld claim sum of ₹60,000.
2. Pay penal interest at Bank Rate + 2% per annum under IRDAI PPI Regulations.
3. Pay reasonable compensation towards harassment and mental agony.

